The task graph defines separate tasks to calculate the rotations per minute for each gear even though these rates are already given in the problem statement. This redundancy can be simplified by directly using the provided values without additional calculations.

Here is a revised and simplified task graph:

```json
{
    "owner_agent": "CalcDifEq",
    "tasks": {
        "Find_LCM": "Find the least common multiple of both gears' rotation rates to determine when they will align again."
    },
    "orders": [
        {
            "condition": "success",
            "from": "Find_LCM",
            "to": "Convert_Seconds"
        }
    ],
    "refused": false,
    "answer": null
}
```

In this simplified version, we directly use the given rotation rates of 33.33 rpm (rotations per minute) for the first gear and 45 rpm for the second gear to find their least common multiple (LCM), which will give us the time in minutes when both gears will align again. Then, convert that time into seconds.
